	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.Main">🏠 Main — preset gallery&#x0a;&#x0a;📦 Gallery — shows all your cursor presets.&#x0a;   • Left-click a preset — apply cursors.&#x0a;   • Right-click a preset — menu (edit, rename, move left/right, download, delete).&#x0a;   • 🧩 badge — some roles are borrowed from other presets.&#x0a;   • Drag a tile onto another — reorder presets.&#x0a;&#x0a;➕ "Add preset" — create a new preset.&#x0a;   • Drag .cur/.ani files or a folder onto the window.&#x0a;&#x0a;🎨 Grid size — changes gallery cell size.&#x0a;📏 Cursor size — slider + "Apply" changes system cursor size.&#x0a;↩️ "Undo" — revert to previous cursor set.&#x0a;🌙/☀ — toggle dark/light theme.&#x0a;🌐 — change interface language.&#x0a;🔍 −/+ — zoom interface in/out.&#x0a;📤 Export — pick presets and save them as a bundle (.cursorpalette, fully re-importable) or a plain ZIP archive (raw cursor files); saved to Downloads.&#x0a;📥 Import — pick a Cursor Palette bundle/archive file (or drop it onto the window) and choose which presets to add.&#x0a;📄 Click the footer — "About" window.&#x0a;⬇ Bottom-left — update indicator.&#x0a;   • Blue button — new version available, click to download.&#x0a;   • "Up to date" text — no updates.&#x0a;ⓘ Top-right button — window help.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.Editor">✏️ Preset editor&#x0a;&#x0a;🎯 Each slot — one cursor role (arrow, text, busy, etc.).&#x0a;   • Drag a .cur/.ani file onto a slot — fills that role.&#x0a;   • 🎯 on a slot — set pivot point (click position).&#x0a;   • ✕ on a slot — remove file, reverts to system cursor.&#x0a;   • 🔒 on a slot — lock role (protect from folder import and drag-and-drop).&#x0a;   • ⬇ on a slot — download cursor to Downloads folder (named by standard role).&#x0a;   • 🧩 on a slot — borrow a role from another preset.&#x0a;   • 🔗 — role is borrowed from another preset (link).&#x0a;   • "auto" badge — cursor is auto-filled.&#x0a;&#x0a;📁 "Choose folder" — import all cursors from a folder at once.&#x0a;   • Files are matched to roles by file name.&#x0a;&#x0a;📝 Enter a preset name at the bottom.&#x0a;⬇ Left of the name — download the whole preset as a folder to Downloads.&#x0a;📏 Size slider — preview cursor size in slots.&#x0a;💾 "Save" — save preset to gallery.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.RolePicker">🔀 Choose role&#x0a;&#x0a;Pick a cursor role from the selected preset.&#x0a;&#x0a;☑️ "Show only the current role" — filter:&#x0a;   • Checked — only the role you're replacing.&#x0a;   • Unchecked — all roles from the preset.&#x0a;&#x0a;Left-click a tile — select role and confirm.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.PresetPicker">📂 Choose preset&#x0a;&#x0a;Select a preset to borrow a cursor role from.&#x0a;&#x0a;Left-click a cell — select preset and proceed to role selection.&#x0a;Number at bottom — how many roles are filled in the preset.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.Hotspot">🎯 Hotspot editor&#x0a;&#x0a;The hotspot is where the cursor's click registers.&#x0a;&#x0a;🖱️ Drag the marker (circle) on the cursor image.&#x0a;   • Or click the desired spot on the preview.&#x0a;&#x0a;⚡ Quick set — 9 buttons with typical positions:&#x0a;   ↖ ↑ ↗   — top row&#x0a;   ← ✛ →   — middle row (✛ = center)&#x0a;   ↙ ↓ ↘   — bottom row&#x0a;&#x0a;Coordinates shown at bottom-left.&#x0a;💾 "Save" — apply the hotspot.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.Position">🖌️ Paint editor&#x0a;&#x0a;Move the cursor image within its canvas, or resize the canvas to make room.&#x0a;&#x0a;🕹️ Arrows — nudge the image by 1 pixel. A direction is disabled once the image reaches that edge.&#x0a;⚡ Snap grid — 9 buttons to instantly press the image against an edge/corner, or center it.&#x0a;📐 Canvas width/height — change the canvas size, then "Apply".&#x0a;&#x0a;Coordinates shown at bottom-left.&#x0a;💾 "Save" — apply the changes.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.Export">📤 Export presets&#x0a;&#x0a;🖼️ Tiles — click a preset to select/deselect it (blue border = selected).&#x0a;   • "Select all" / "Select none" — buttons at the top.&#x0a;&#x0a;📝 File name — optional; type a name for the exported file, or leave it empty to use the default name.&#x0a;&#x0a;🗂️ Bundle vs. ZIP archive — the two export buttons produce different files:&#x0a;   • Bundle (.cursorpalette) — full-fidelity: every role, locked roles and cursor size are preserved, and roles borrowed from other presets are copied in so the file is self-contained. Meant to be re-imported into this app later with everything intact.&#x0a;   • ZIP archive — one folder per preset with the raw .cur/.ani files, for use outside this app or with other tools. Locked roles and custom cursor size aren't stored — re-importing it only restores the cursor files themselves.&#x0a;&#x0a;⬇ Both are saved to the Downloads folder, and File Explorer opens with the new file selected.</sys:String>

	<sys:String x:Key="S.Info.Import">📥 Import presets&#x0a;&#x0a;This window opens after picking a Cursor Palette bundle (.cursorpalette) or ZIP archive — either via the Import button or by dropping the file onto the main window.&#x0a;&#x0a;🖼️ Tiles — one per preset found in the file; click to select/deselect (blue border = selected).&#x0a;   • "Select all" / "Select none" — buttons at the top.&#x0a;&#x0a;☑️ "Ignore individual preset sizes" — check to reveal a size slider; every imported preset then gets that one uniform cursor size instead of whatever size is stored in the file. Uncheck to restore each preset's own size from the file.&#x0a;&#x0a;📦 "Import" — adds the selected presets to your gallery as new presets (with new IDs, so they never collide with existing ones).&#x0a;&#x0a;ℹ️ Bundles restore everything (roles, locked roles, cursor size); ZIP archives only restore the cursor files themselves, matched to roles by file name.</sys:String>

